  "limitations": [
    "Only nonempty ordinary uncompressed magic 2 batches are admitted. Legacy/compressed/transaction/control/idempotent/delete-horizon/log-append-time features remain typed unsupported and unadvertised.",
    "This is a stricter admission subset, not a general Fetch/compaction decoder: positive counts, contiguous in-batch deltas, canonical varints, valid UTF-8 header keys and complete-input consumption are required.",
    "Batch base offsets are checked independently; producer batches commonly each start at zero. A future handler must assign offsets and enforce signed offset/topic/authorization/timestamp/Produce policy.",
    "The independent Apache evidence executes low-level official builders/parsers, not a running Kafka broker or LogValidator. Upstream parser acceptance is not broker acceptance. Exact differing outcomes are retained.",
    "Native codec jars are external oracle-only dependencies. This task changes neither broker/client manifests nor client record code/default dependency graph.",
    "CRC32C detects corruption and does not authenticate adversarial rewriting. Limits bound bytes/work/retained validator state, not process RSS or caller-retained input/concurrency.",
    "The journal composition inherits its synchronous blocking-executor, cross-process ownership and Linux directory-sync filesystem contracts. Restart tests do not qualify physical power loss, network filesystems, replication or production durability.",
    "Full integrated source tests pass including optional TLS, but the records foundation implements no Produce handler/advertisement, acknowledgements, replicas, transactions, sequencing or broker qualification."
  ],
